-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/e15dbcfe-1bfe-4245-9502-9b69cb685229
-- title:
--   Lemma 2.4: Kazhdan constant bounds $\lambda_{\max}$ of the averaging operator (corrected: $|S|\ge2$)
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a compact group, $S=(S_i)_{i\in\iota}$ a finite family of elements closed under taking inverses, and $\rho$ a finite-dimensional continuous unitary representation of $G$. Write
--   $$
--   A = \frac1{|S|}\sum_{i\in\iota}\rho(S_i),\qquad E = \mathbb E_{g\sim\mu(G)}\rho(g)
--   $$
--   with $\mu(G)$ the Haar probability measure, and let $K(G;S)$ be the Kazhdan constant. Then:
--
--   1. if $|S|\ge 2$,
--   $$
--   \lambda_{\max}(A-E) \le 1-\frac{K(G;S)^2}{2|S|} ;
--   $$
--   2. if $S$ contains the identity, the same bound holds for the operator norm $\|A-E\|$.
--
--   This converts a lower bound on the Kazhdan constant into a one-sided spectral gap; with Theorem 2.11 and Lemma 2.12 it gives Theorem 2.3.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\lambda_{\max}(X)\le c$ for the Hermitian $X=A-E$ is stated as $\mathrm{Re}\langle v,Xv\rangle\le c\|v\|^2$ for all $v$. Closure under inverses is an involution $\sigma$ of the index set with $S_{\sigma(i)}=S_i^{-1}$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - correction: λ_max bound (2.14) for every S → λ_max clause assumes |S| ≥ 2; reason: printed statement false: G = ℤ/2, S = {g}, ρ trivial gives λ_max(A − E) = 0 > 1 − K²/2 = −1 (K(ℤ/2; {g}) = 2)
--   - generalization: a subset S closed under inverses → an indexed family closed under inverses (an involution σ of the index set with S_{σ i} = S_i⁻¹); reason: a subset closed under inverses is the family indexed by itself; the proof works with multiplicity
--   - generalization: G compact (finite or Lie) and generated by S → G any compact Hausdorff topological group; S need not generate G; reason: the bound holds without generation (then K(G;S) = 0 or the bound is unchanged) and without the Lie structure; it specializes to the source
--   - encoding: λ_max(A − E) ≤ c → Re⟨v, (A − E)v⟩ ≤ c‖v‖² for all v; reason: A − E is Hermitian (S closed under inverses, E an orthogonal projector); equivalent
--   - reading: K(G; S) (not defined in the paper) and representations of a compact group → K over finite-dimensional continuous unitary representations without nonzero invariant vectors (one infimum of attained values); ρ continuous; reason: the paper defers to [CHH+24, §2.4]; continuity is the standing convention for representations of a compact group
-- source:
--   Anshu–Balasubramanian–Haferkamp–Harrow–Tan, Depth-1 expanders on the unitary group and applications, arXiv:2609.01605 (held version, sha256 3c3f8513…aebfd87), Lemma 2.4, Eq. (2.14), p.9 (cited from [CHH+24, Lemma 2.17])

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ConstGapCircuits_compactGroups
import Definitions.Def_ConstGapCircuits_spectralGap
import Definitions.Def_DepthOneQExp_kazhdan

namespace DepthOneQExp

open scoped InnerProductSpace

/-- Lemma 2.4 ([CHH+24, Lemma 2.17]) (Anshu–Balasubramanian–Haferkamp–Harrow–Tan, *Depth-1
expanders on the unitary group and applications*, arXiv:2609.01605, held version sha256
3c3f8513…aebfd87, Lemma 2.4, Eq. (2.14), p.9), with the correction `|S| ≥ 2` in the first clause.
Let `G` be a compact group, `S = (S_i)_{i ∈ ι}` a finite family closed under taking inverses, `ρ` a
finite-dimensional unitary representation, `A = (1/|S|) Σ_i ρ(S_i)` and `E = E_{g∼µ(G)} ρ(g)`
(Haar probability). Then
(a) if `|S| ≥ 2`, `λ_max(A − E) ≤ 1 − K(G; S)² / (2|S|)`;
(b) if `S` contains the identity, `‖A − E‖ ≤ 1 − K(G; S)² / (2|S|)`.

**Formalization Note** `λ_max(X) ≤ c` for the Hermitian `X = A − E` is stated as the Rayleigh bound
`Re⟨v, X v⟩ ≤ c ‖v‖²` for all `v`. Closure under inverses is an involution `σ` of the index set
with `S_{σ i} = S_i⁻¹` (a subset closed under inverses is the family indexed by itself). The
paper's "generated by `S`" and "(finite or Lie)" are not assumed. `K` is `kazhdan`. -/
theorem lemma_2_4 {G : Type} [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G] [IsTopologicalGroup G]
    [CompactSpace G] [T2Space G] [MeasurableSpace G] [BorelSpace G]
    {ι : Type} [Fintype ι] (S : ι → G) (hS : ∃ σ : ι ≃ ι, ∀ i, S (σ i) = (S i)⁻¹)
    (ρ : ConstGapCircuits.UnitaryRep G) :
    (2 ≤ Fintype.card ι → ∀ v : EuclideanSpace ℂ (Fin ρ.dim),
      RCLike.re ⟪v, Matrix.toEuclideanCLM (𝕜 := ℂ)
          ((1 / (Fintype.card ι : ℂ)) • ∑ i, (ρ.hom (S i) : Matrix (Fin ρ.dim) (Fin ρ.dim) ℂ) -
            ConstGapCircuits.invariantProjector ρ) v⟫_ℂ ≤
        (1 - kazhdan G S ^ 2 / (2 * Fintype.card ι)) * ‖v‖ ^ 2) ∧
    ((∃ i, S i = 1) →
      ConstGapCircuits.opNorm
          ((1 / (Fintype.card ι : ℂ)) • ∑ i, (ρ.hom (S i) : Matrix (Fin ρ.dim) (Fin ρ.dim) ℂ) -
            ConstGapCircuits.invariantProjector ρ) ≤
        1 - kazhdan G S ^ 2 / (2 * Fintype.card ι)) := by sorry

end DepthOneQExp
